From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:51:57 +0200
Subject: video: the window texture in the application's format when the
 renderer has it

The streaming texture behind the SDL 1.2 screen surface was always made in
the renderer's first format. The OpenGL renderer lists ARGB8888 first, and
a 32-bit SDL 1.2 screen is XRGB8888, so every update converted the frame
into the texture (SDL_UpperBlit into VideoConvertSurface20). With SSE
that is cheap; on the PS3 (PowerPC, AltiVec) it was 11% of Warmux's frame
after the alpha blits. Now, when the renderer lists the application's own
format, the texture is made in it and an update is a plain copy; other
formats convert as before.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/SDL12_compat.c b/src/SDL12_compat.c
--- a/src/SDL12_compat.c
+++ b/src/SDL12_compat.c
@@ -6824,6 +6824,20 @@ SetVideoModeImpl(int width, int height, int bpp, Uint32 flags12)
             return EndVidModeCreate();
         }
 
+        /* Walnut: the texture in the application's own format when the renderer has it, else its
+           first one as before. The first (ARGB8888) against the 32-bit screen's XRGB8888 meant a
+           whole-frame conversion on every update: 11% of Warmux's frame on the PS3 (no SSE there). */
+        {
+            Uint32 k;
+            /* 32-bit formats only: an INDEX8 texture would need the palette set on it */
+            for (k = 0; SDL_BYTESPERPIXEL(appfmt) == 4 && k < rinfo.num_texture_formats; k++) {
+                if (rinfo.texture_formats[k] == appfmt) {
+                    rinfo.texture_formats[0] = appfmt;
+                    break;
+                }
+            }
+        }
+
         if (!VideoTexture20) {
             SDL20_SetHint(SDL_HINT_RENDER_SCALE_QUALITY, WantScaleMethodNearest ? "0" : "1");
             VideoTexture20 = SDL20_CreateTexture(VideoRenderer20, rinfo.texture_formats[0], SDL_TEXTUREACCESS_STREAMING, width, height);
